; `return` of a wider integer than the routine declares takes its cast, as a
; binding, an assignment and an argument always did. Until 2026-11-10 the
; return positions never asked: f(4294967303) answered 7 at rc 0.
; Planner.report_return_narrowing#.
; xfail: the returned value narrows int into i32

function f(big: int) returns i32
{
    return big
}

if (f(4294967303) as int) = 7
    print "PASS"
